<article class="env-proposition" id="BC1240">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/BC1240">Proposition <span data-tag="BC1240">1.2.4.3</span> <span class="named">(Joyal <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/joyalnotpub">joyalnotpub</a>]</span>)</span>.</a>equivalence!in an $\infty $-category Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category, and $\phi : \Delta ^1 \rightarrow \calC $ a morphism of $\calC $. Then $\phi $ is an equivalence if and only if, for every $n \geq 2$ and every map $f_0: \Lambda ^ n_0 \rightarrow \calC $ such that $f_0 | \Delta ^{\{ 0,1\} } = \phi $, there exists an extension of $f_0$ to $\Delta ^ n$. </p>
